; The F6.2 extraction benchmark. Nothing in this directory *runs* under a plain
; [dune runtest] except the corpus-integrity check: the metric runner needs the
; Python venv and measures time and memory, which is an operator's run, not a
; gate step (plans/ocaml-finalisation.md, F6.2). What the gate does check is the
; recorded quality bar, in [../../test/corpus_html/], and that the corpus is
; still exactly what its generator writes.

; The metric definitions and the bar live here, in [extract_metrics.ml]: the gate
; rule beside the corpus in [../test/corpus_html/dune] and the table mode below
; both run this one program, so a bar means the same thing in both. It links the
; backend it measures, which is the whole point — a metric that no longer compiles
; against [Extractor] is a metric that stopped meaning anything.
(library
 (name extract_metrics)
 (modules extract_metrics)
 (libraries seekwright.fetch seekwright.fetch.stdlib yojson))

; The fixture generator. It writes the corpus under [../../test/corpus_html/]
; when given a directory to write into; [gen_fixtures --check <dir>] re-derives
; every fixture and the manifest in memory and fails when a checked-in file no
; longer matches, so a fixture can only change by changing the program that
; makes it. [runtest] runs the check mode, with the corpus declared as deps so
; the sandbox carries it.
(executable
 (name gen_fixtures)
 (modules gen_fixtures)
 (libraries yojson unix))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  gen_fixtures.exe
  (glob_files ../../test/corpus_html/fixtures/*)
  ../../test/corpus_html/cases.json)
 (action (run ./gen_fixtures.exe --check ../../test/corpus_html)))

; The OCaml half of the metric table: runs the port's [stdlib] backend over the
; corpus and prints one metric row per case as JSON. [yojson] builds the row,
; [unix] is the wall clock and the GC counters. The operator commands are in the
; header of [bench.ml], and [metrics_table.py] puts the three backends' rows
; into the table that gets recorded.
(executable
 (name bench)
 (modules bench)
 (libraries extract_metrics yojson unix))


; The identity check behind a plumbing change: a digest of what the backend
; answers for every corpus case, and the phase timings of one case.
(executable
 (name digest_cases)
 (modules digest_cases)
 (libraries seekwright.fetch seekwright.fetch.stdlib extract_metrics))
